# Dialogue
@scenario tutorial_lesson_01
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char pip global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show pip guide listen]
pip: This is dialogue. In VNS, write the character ID, a colon, and the words you want them to say.
pip: Open this lesson's .vns file, change this sentence, and run it again.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
pip: Which line displays dialogue?
> pip: Hello! -> correct
> @label start_here -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show pip guide curious]
pip: A speaker ID before a colon makes a dialogue line. A label names a place to jump. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show pip guide cheer]
pip: A speaker ID before a colon makes a dialogue line. A label names a place to jump.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_01]
[flag tutorial_done_01]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_1]
